<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William Howard Taft</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1857–1930</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William Howard Taft was an American lawyer and politician who headed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippine-commission">Philippine Commission</a> from 1900 and became the first civilian governor-general of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a> in 1901. As secretary of war he briefly served as provisional governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a> in 1906. He was president of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> from 1909 to 1913 and chief justice from 1921 to 1930.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-howard-taft.jpg" alt="William Howard Taft" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pach Brothers, restored by Adam Cuerden · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:William_Howard_Taft_by_Pach_Brothers_(3x4_ropped)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
